{
    "metadata": {
        "name": "ShaderPlayer Dark",
        "revision": 1,
        "license": "SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT",
        "copyright": [
            "ShaderPlayer editor theme, authored from the token table in src/ui/Theme.h."
        ]
    },

    "_comment": [
        "This file is the ONE place the token colours are repeated for the editor.",
        "src/ui/HlslHighlighter.cpp and src/ui/EditorPanel.cpp write no colour of their",
        "own: the gutter, the current-line band, the brace match and the error mark all",
        "read their colour back out of the editor-colors block below. Change a value here",
        "and in src/ui/Theme.h together, or in neither.",
        "",
        "Syntax colours follow one rule the reader can learn in a second: azure is the",
        "language grammar, cyan its types, lime the intrinsics fxc provides, amber the",
        "numbers, rose the strings, violet the preprocessor. Anything left near-white is",
        "the author's own code. Magenta (#FF5FD2) never appears here because nothing in a",
        "grammar can know it: HlslHighlighter paints the injected-preamble identifiers in",
        "it as a second pass, so an unfamiliar name is instantly placeable as this",
        "application's rather than the file's."
    ],

    "text-styles": {
        "Normal": {
            "text-color": "#ECECEC",
            "selected-text-color": "#06181B"
        },
        "Keyword": {
            "text-color": "#5AA8FF",
